# ci-pool-attributed-gauges.timer — the pool's per-repository gauges, about
# every minute.
#
# WHY ITS OWN TIMER, and not a faster lifecycle sweep. The obvious way to get
# these numbers to a live board would be to speed up
# scan-runner-pod-lifecycle.timer, which already makes the ClusterQueue read.
# That is wrong: the sweep's journal, scheduler-event and containerd.log reads
# are all bounded to a 5-minute look-back window precisely so consecutive
# sweeps TILE the timeline without double-counting, and its unit budgets 240 s
# for one run. Dropping it to a minute would double-count its classes and
# overrun its own deadline. So the attributed gauges ride a separate,
# much cheaper unit: four bounded kubectl list calls and two loopback POSTs.
#
# THIS INTERVAL IS ALSO THE START SIGNAL'S DEDUP WINDOW. The per-phase start
# emission (`livespec-ifwnqj.6`) keeps no state between ticks; it reports a
# start only while the workflow pod is younger than CI_POOL_START_WINDOW_S,
# which defaults to this 60 s. Change one and the other has to move with it,
# or a start is either reported twice or not at all.
#
# ONE MINUTE because the reader is a live board (the plan's H2,
# `livespec-mqy35a`) watched while jobs start and finish, and a 5-minute
# granularity cannot show a queue filling and draining inside one workflow
# run. AccuracySec=1s keeps systemd from coalescing the tick into a wider
# window, which at a 60 s interval it otherwise would.
#
# OnBootSec sits after the boot converge (../k3s/phase2/reconstruct/
# converge-ci-stack.service, ~2.5 min from an empty datastore) so the first
# tick after a reboot reads a cluster that HAS its ClusterQueues and scale
# sets, rather than emitting nothing and leaving a red unit for the next tick
# to heal. Persistent=false: a missed minute of a live board is not worth
# replaying a stale reading on the next boot, unlike the 5-minute sweeps.
[Unit]
Description=CI runner pool per-repository queue and runner gauges (every minute)

[Timer]
OnBootSec=5min
OnUnitActiveSec=1min
AccuracySec=1s
Persistent=false

[Install]
WantedBy=timers.target
